+    // ── TL-042 Option-1 (AW/W-unaccepted synthetic-accept recovery) PROTOTYPE ──
+    // Scratch prototype (docs/DIAGNOSE_XHB500_RAW_HREADYOUT_LOW.md Option 1).
+    // On the XHB500 write-wedge where an AW is presented on s_axi but the
+    // downstream Wlink target never asserts awready, the existing synth-B backstop
+    // is blind (it arms on sub_wr_os_ctr!=0 = ACCEPTED AWs). These nets let the
+    // wrapper synthesise the AW/W accept into the bridge at the stall timeout and
+    // then reuse the existing synth-B drain. The REAL downstream awready/wready
+    // (s_axi_awready / s_axi_wready) stay the Wlink-driven nets; the bridge is fed
